date: 2026-07-25
host: Apple M4 Pro (12 cores), macOS 26.5.2
target: aarch64-apple-darwin
rustc: 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14)
harness: zenav1-aom-dsp-bench / dsp_kernels (zenbench 0.1.9), port-only, no C oracle
before_commit: 4b92e2b   # clean tree in a sibling worktree; aarch64 had NO transform vector path
after_commit: (this landing — transform SIMD as one magetypes body, NEON tier live + half_batch_pays gate)
baseline_name: arm-pre-neon

commands:
  # before (sibling worktree at 4b92e2b)
  nice -n 19 cargo bench -q -p zenav1-aom-dsp-bench --bench dsp_kernels -- --save-baseline=arm-pre-neon
  # then copy crates/aom-dsp-bench/.zenbench/baselines/arm-pre-neon.json into the main checkout
  # after
  nice -n 19 cargo bench -q -p zenav1-aom-dsp-bench --bench dsp_kernels -- --baseline=arm-pre-neon

notes:
  - AOM_FORCE_SCALAR=1 is NOT a scalar baseline on aarch64 (neon is a
    compile-time-guaranteed archmage token and cannot be disabled outside test
    builds), so this is a two-BUILD pair, not a pinned/unpinned pair.
  - 43 non-transform cells (cdef/loopfilter/dist/quant/intra) run code this
    landing does not touch and serve as the negative control:
    min -16.2% / p50 +0.7% / p90 +4.6% / max +12.0%.
  - Parity gates that had to be green before timing anything: in-module
    SIMD-vs-scalar differential 25 permutations / 24 with a vector tier;
    txfm2d_simd_perm_diff simd_perms=24 scalar_perms=1; the C-oracle transform
    differentials; full aom-dsp suite 352/352 in both dispatch modes.
